# Realtime

- Publish only canonical events derived from committed state.
- Use at-least-once delivery semantics; never assume exactly-once transport.
- Include contract version, event ID, stream ID, and revision in durable events.
- Deduplicate by event ID and apply only contiguous stream revisions.
- Stop incremental application on a gap; replay or replace with an authorized snapshot.
- Reauthenticate reconnects and reauthorize each subscription.
- Filter hidden data server-side before events or snapshots leave the API.
- Separate ephemeral presence from durable game state.
- Bound queues and apply explicit slow-consumer/disconnect policy.
- Test duplicates, gaps, out-of-order delivery, reconnect, and revoked access.
